---
const faqs = [
  {
    question: "How do we determine the right screen size and pixel pitch for our property?",
    answer: "Pixel pitch (e.g., P2.5 vs. P4.0) is determined strictly by your property's minimum viewing distance: each millimetre of pitch corresponds to approximately one metre of viewing distance. Sizing depends on gatehouse boom geometry or mall atrium scale. During our on-site feasibility assessment, our technicians measure exact sightlines, approach speeds, and ambient lux so you never overpay for unneeded pixel density."
  },
  {
    question: "Does the outdoor display comply with municipal outdoor advertising by-laws and curfews?",
    answer: "Yes. South African municipal by-laws (including the City of Cape Town Outdoor Advertising By-law and George Municipality by-laws) enforce strict luminance caps and curfews. Our outdoor displays include factory-calibrated ambient lux sensors that automatically dim the screen at dusk (capping output below municipal thresholds like 1,000 cd/m²) to prevent glare and comply with environmental dark-sky regulations."
  },
  {
    question: "How does an estate installation satisfy Body Corporate PMR 29 and HOA approval?",
    answer: "Under the Sectional Titles Schemes Management Act (STSMA Act 8 of 2011), permanent displays are classified as improvements to common property. By configuring the screen primarily for essential community utility—gatehouse security notices, municipal water/load-shedding alerts, and AGM reminders—the installation qualifies under Prescribed Management Rule 29(2) as a 'reasonably necessary' improvement requiring only a 30-day trustee notice rather than a unanimous vote under PMR 29(1). We furnish board-ready itemised proposals suitable for trustee and AGM distribution."
  },
  {
    question: "Who manages the structural steelwork, wind loading, and electrical compliance?",
    answer: "We deliver complete turnkey installation accountability. Our team coordinates custom structural bracket mounting engineered to SANS 10160 wind-load standards (critical for Cape coastal winds), safe concealed power cabling, dedicated sub-distribution breakers, and certified electrical compliance under SANS 10142-1 (issuing a formal electrical Certificate of Compliance / CoC upon sign-off)."
  },
  {
    question: "How complex is daily content scheduling for non-technical office staff?",
    answer: "No dedicated IT personnel or graphic designers are required. Our cloud CMS runs in any desktop or mobile browser. Estate managers or mall marketing teams can select from pre-formatted notice templates, schedule automated dayparted playlists (e.g. morning traffic alerts vs. evening AGM notices), and publish updates in under 90 seconds. We conduct comprehensive operator training upon handover."
  },
  {
    question: "Can our property use optional advertising slots to offset the capital expenditure?",
    answer: "Yes, where permitted by estate rules or commercial landlord policies. For shopping centres and mixed-use precincts, commercial advertising slots provide substantial recurring non-GLA revenue. For residential estates, trustees frequently approve vetted local community service sponsors (security providers, local schools, or estate golf clubs) to subsidise display CapEx without compromising estate aesthetic integrity."
  }
];
---

<section class="section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">Pre-Assessment Answers</span>
      <h2 id="faq-heading" class="section-title">
        Frequently Asked Questions Before Booking a Site Visit
      </h2>
      <p class="section-desc">
        Direct answers to technical, statutory, and commercial governance questions commonly evaluated by managing agents, trustees, and commercial asset managers.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- FAQ Accordion List -->
    <div class="faq-list" role="region" aria-label="Frequently Asked Questions">
      {faqs.map((faq, index) => (
        <details class="faq-item" name="faq-group">
          <summary class="faq-question">
            <span class="faq-index tabular-num">0{index + 1}</span>
            <span class="faq-title">{faq.question}</span>
            <span class="faq-chevron" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/>
              </svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
    max-width: 860px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .faq-item {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-primary);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: border-color 0.15s ease, box-shadow 0.15s ease;
  }

  .faq-item:hover {
    border-color: rgba(36, 99, 184, 0.4);
  }

  .faq-item[open] {
    border-color: var(--color-brand-primary);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
  }

  .faq-question {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    min-height: 44px;
    cursor: pointer;
    user-select: none;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .faq-question::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-index {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-brand-primary);
    font-weight: 700;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .faq-title {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    flex-grow: 1;
  }

  .faq-chevron {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    transition: transform 0.2s ease;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .faq-item[open] .faq-chevron {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
    color: var(--color-brand-primary);
  }

  .faq-answer {
    padding: 0 1.5rem 1.5rem 3.5rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(226, 232, 240, 0.5);
    padding-top: 1rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .faq-question {
      padding: 1rem;
    }
    .faq-answer {
      padding: 0.75rem 1rem 1rem 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
